                                "example_id": "4d34f2ed-7956-44c3-8934-6f52ac73ea25",
                                "sense_id": "5551b121-a644-3398-aeaa-0d3bfe8cd770",
                                "text": "I am not sure how our \"gentle-hearted\" little girl will take the sight of the sheep's death, but when it happens she seems as matter-of-fact as the other two children."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "20b2fa67-f555-3d3f-a23b-0184d6dd67bc",
                        "entry_id": "fb393959-26d3-3b0e-8bfb-e0c09dd176d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Meek and mild."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "28e722d1-147c-4ce9-b819-a681930f5d3f",
                                "sense_id": "20b2fa67-f555-3d3f-a23b-0184d6dd67bc",
                                "text": "Were these that worshipped here more reverential of the dead? or more affectionate in attachments unsevered by the grave? or more abundant in resources to procure what gentle-hearted poverty might sigh for in vain, a monument, or tablet, or grave stone;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e57d4bb-b65b-4527-99e3-c3fc8d1c86bd",
                                "sense_id": "20b2fa67-f555-3d3f-a23b-0184d6dd67bc",
                                "text": "The officials shall go on addressing the troops and say, \"Is there anyone afraid or gentle-hearted? Let him go back to his home, lest he melt the heart of his brothers, like his heart!\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b12b493a-0233-3bea-96db-fa8ce402bbfd",
                        "entry_id": "fb393959-26d3-3b0e-8bfb-e0c09dd176d4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Refined and cultivated, high-born"
                        ],
